; A `(pass …)` whose `post()` is commented out.
;
; The fourth site of the comment blindness §407 fixed at the other three, and
; the only one that is not a binding: `extractPostFunction` walked the body for
; the substring `@fragment`, so the disabled text below still built a second
; shader module, a second pipeline and a second render pass — and THAT pass, not
; `fs`, is what reached the canvas. The document rendered the inverted image at
; exit 0, with two W0003 warnings (`samp` and `postTex` declared and never used
; in the main module) as the only sign anything was wrong.
;
; The extractor reads `wgsl_scan`'s trivia and entry points now, so this is one
; pass drawing one gradient. (journal §408.)
(pass-graph
  (pass :name main :code """
    @fragment fn fs(@builtin(position) pos: vec4f) -> @location(0) vec4f {
      let uv = pos.xy / vec2f(pngine.width, pngine.height);
      return vec4f(uv, sin(pngine.time) * .5 + .5, 1);
    }

    /* Disabled while the gradient is tuned:
    @fragment fn post(@builtin(position) pos: vec4f) -> @location(0) vec4f {
      let c = textureLoad(postTex, vec2i(pos.xy), 0);
      return vec4f(1. - c.rgb, 1.);
    }
    */
  """))
